# Database migrations must be registered in setup.sh

Deployments only auto-apply migrations listed in `apply_required_database_migrations()` inside `james-newsystem/setup.sh`. A migration file under `api/migrations/` is **not** enough on its own.

## When adding or changing a migration

1. Add the SQL file under `api/migrations/` using the next sequential number (e.g. `030_description.sql`).
2. **In the same change**, append that file to the `migrations=( ... )` array in `james-newsystem/setup.sh`, keeping numeric order.
3. Prefer idempotent SQL (`IF NOT EXISTS`, safe `ALTER` patterns) because `setup.sh` may re-run migrations on update.

## Example

```bash
# james-newsystem/setup.sh — inside apply_required_database_migrations()
local migrations=(
  ...
  "$API_DIR/migrations/029_add_call_report_call_details.sql"
  "$API_DIR/migrations/030_your_new_migration.sql"  # ← add every new migration here
)
```

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] New file exists in `api/migrations/`
- [ ] Same PR/commit updates `james-newsystem/setup.sh`
- [ ] Migration filename matches the setup.sh entry exactly

If you add a migration without updating `setup.sh`, call that out explicitly — deploy/update will skip it.
